        "failure_scenario": "A raw threads object containing id t, category social, a conflict marker with social/promotions, and a messages array with sender/subject/date/INBOX is passed through normalizeSearchThreads then applyCategories with promoIds [t]. Observed output is category promotions, hasUnsubscribe true and no marker; a sender-plus-hasUnsubscribe trash match returns true. The new references/gmail.md promise that ingest accepts existing explicit fields and that re-ingesting markers cannot erase uncertainty does not hold through this CLI path. The stripping line predates the diff; this is a candidate missing integration under the approved plan's existing-evidence policy, whose applicability to raw inputs should be verified.",
        "quote": "out.push({\n      id: t.id,\n      from: first.sender ?? null,\n      subject: first.subject ?? null,\n      date: first.date ?? null,\n      labelIds: [...new Set(msgs.flatMap((m) => m?.labelIds ?? []))],\n    });",
